Clockwork (Clockwork 1)
https://github.com/hiddentao/clockwork-engine
Copyright (c) Ramesh Nair
MIT License

Clockwork 2 is a clean-room successor to Clockwork 1. It keeps that project's
architecture - seeded PRNG, tick timers, input-log recording, deterministic
replay, headless validation - and changes the timing model from variable-step
to fixed-step. It has a fresh git history and is not a fork.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
alea
https://github.com/coverslide/node-alea
Copyright (c) 2010 Johannes Baagoe
MIT License

packages/kernel/src/prng/alea.ts is a vendored TypeScript transcription of
alea 1.0.1. It is vendored rather than depended upon so that the kernel has
no runtime dependencies. Its output is proved byte-identical to the published
package by packages/kernel/tests/prng/alea-parity.test.ts.

